---
/**
 * terms-of-use.astro — 使用条款
 *
 * 写作红线：本站是制造商的产品资料页，不是工程顾问。所以条款必须明确
 * 「页面参数是参考值、最终以报价单与确认图为准」—— 这与 companyProfile.termsNote
 * 的口径保持一致，也是产品页规格表已经在用的措辞。
 * 不虚构争议解决机制之外的细节；管辖法律按公司注册地写。
 *
 * ⚠️ 由代码与商务条款事实整理而成，不构成法律意见；对外使用前应请法务/律师复核。
 */
import DocPage from "../layouts/DocPage.astro";
import { companyFacts, termsNote } from "../lib/companyProfile";
---

<DocPage
    pageTitle="Terms of Use"
    description="The terms governing use of MEIYU Aluminum's website: product information status, intellectual property, disclaimers and liability."
    titleWhite="Terms of"
    titleGold="Use"
    eyebrow="Legal"
    subtitle="The ground rules for using this website and the information on it."
>
    <h2>Acceptance</h2>
    <p>
        By using <strong>{Astro.site?.host}</strong> you agree to these terms. If
        you do not agree, please do not use the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Status of the information on this site</h2>
    <p>This is the most important point, so we state it plainly:</p>
    <div class="doc-note">
        Specification tables, finish descriptions, perforation patterns, fire
        ratings, weights and installation guidance on this site are <strong
            >indicative product information</strong
        >, not engineering specifications for your project. Confirmed figures —
        including alloy, temper, gauge, coating system, panel dimensions,
        tolerances and fixing details — are those issued with your quotation and
        approved shop drawings.
    </div>
    <p>
        {termsNote} Curtain wall, facade and ceiling systems must be designed and
        verified by a qualified engineer for the specific building, load case and
        local code. Nothing on this site substitutes for that.
    </p>

    <h2>Prices and lead times</h2>
    <p>
        Any figures shown for MOQ, lead time or warranty describe our standard
        offer and are confirmed at quotation. They are not standing price quotes
        and expire with the quotation that carries them.
    </p>

    <h2>Your submissions</h2>
    <p>
        When you send us an enquiry, drawings or a project brief, you keep
        ownership of them. You grant us permission to use them only to prepare
        and price what you asked for. Please do not send confidential material
        without telling us.
    </p>

    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
        The site text, layout and original photography are owned by
        {companyFacts.name}. Product photographs show our own production where
        marked as such; rendered and illustrative images are used to explain
        construction and are not records of completed projects. Downloaded
        material may be used inside your own organisation for evaluation and
        specification; it may not be republished commercially or presented as
        your own.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party links</h2>
    <p>
        Where we link to standards bodies, test references or our YouTube
        channel, we do not control and are not responsible for those sites.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty on the site itself</h2>
    <p>
        The site is provided "as is". We do not warrant that it is
        uninterrupted, error-free, or that every page reflects the current
        product catalogue — some ranges are updated in the catalogue ahead of
        the website.
    </p>

    <h2>Limits of liability</h2>
    <p>
        To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for losses arising
        from reliance on website information alone. Contractual responsibility
        for supplied goods is governed by the quotation, purchase order and
        applicable standards referenced in them.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China,
        where
        {companyFacts.name} is established. Supply contracts may specify a different
        governing law; the contract documents prevail.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
        We may update these terms as the site or our product range changes. The
        date below shows the last revision.
    </p>

    <p class="doc-updated">
        Last updated: October 2026 · Questions to
        <a href={`mailto:${companyFacts.email}`}>{companyFacts.email}</a>
    </p>
</DocPage>
